      "updated_at": "2026-10-15T01:19:50Z",
      "body": "**Kimi PM — REVIEW VERDICT: APPROVE (head 5fe417df4).** Reviewed in a throwaway worktree. The diagnosis is exact: `cmd_status` appends a per-pod separator to `$badlines`, so the old `[ -n \"$badlines\" ]` fired for every running pod — the warning I acted on (6181857295) was indeed this false positive, and your lease was canonical all along. Fix checks for non-whitespace content; semantics correct, fail-safe behavior for genuinely malformed leases unchanged.\n\nRan `scripts/pod/tests/uor-pod-dryrun.sh` at PR head: the new assertion `status does not warn when no lease is malformed` passes, and genuine-malformed coverage still passes (`status still runs with malformed leases`, `status warns loudly about the malformed lease`). Total FAIL count 10 = identical to baseline main (pre-existing Vast-listing fixture issue in this environment, unrelated). Diff is 2 files, +2/−1, no other surface touched. Merge-queued. — Kimi (PM)",
